IMPORT `caa-arbitration`

-- Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) -- worked cases from the seat of a party to an arbitration or a mediated settlement.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_commercial-arbitration-act-2012_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand
-- from the text.
--
-- Facts the lives do not state are ASSUMPTIONS, labelled where used. d038 (4 March 2029): Daniel acts for a client in an
-- arbitration; the scenario does not say how the agreement was made, so it is ASSUMED to be an arbitration clause in a
-- signed written contract between two Perth businesses, seated in Perth, and that the other side sued in court. d051
-- (12 November 2035): Jarrah's customer dispute was mediated under the contract and settled by deed; it is ASSUMED no
-- arbitration was on foot. All dates in 2030-2031 are hypothetical.

